# Model routing (Win11 + Cursor)

**Golden rule:** if `pwsh octo.ps1 -Pipeline <phase> -Action run` solves it, do not call an LLM.

| Phase | Cursor mode | Model | Escalation |
|-------|-------------|-------|------------|
| `/scan` | Agent | `composer-2.5-fast` | — |
| `/model` (Phase A) | Plan | `gpt-5.6-terra-medium` | `claude-sonnet-5-thinking-high` only if card >15 files |
| Execute (Phase B) | Agent | `composer-2.5-fast` | `gpt-5.6-terra-medium` after 2 retries on same step |
| `/ship` | Agent | `gpt-5.6-terra-medium` (verdict turn) | `composer-2.5-fast` when ship is scripts-only |
| `/close` | Agent | `composer-2.5-fast` | card-lite is script — no LLM needed |
| `/review` | Ask | `composer-2.5-fast` | — |
| `/debug` | Agent | `gpt-5.6-terra-medium` | thinking only after 2 failed hypotheses |
| `/prompt` (meta) | Ask | `gpt-5.6-terra-medium` | `composer-2.5-fast` for trivial one-file rewrites |

## Rules

- Model switch is **manual in the picker** — Cursor exposes no programmatic switch. Commands state the target model; the operator switches at phase boundaries.
- 1 chat = 1 card. Switch fast↔balanced at phase boundaries, never mid-step.
- Policy over instance: fast default for execution, one balanced model for `/model` + `/ship` verdicts. Model names above are the current instance — update here when the catalog changes.
- COST 0 stack always runs first: scan bootstrap, context-search, read-gate, gates, ship orchestrator, card-lite.
